<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France braces for new wave of protests, govt warns of 'very high' violence risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07757db6f5eabf0cd43c2fd56d5eb5621329887f5b08028728cf63419f77f235</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:35:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-france-braces-for-new-wave-of-protests-govt-warns-of-very-high-violence-risk" /><summary type="html">France's interior minister on Thursday warned of a "very high risk of public disorder" and announced the deployment of around 70,000 police officers for a new wave of protests this weekend. France has been rocked by widespread anger over the rising cost of living and inequality, with nationwide demonstrations on October 17 degenerating into some of the country's worst rioting in years. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Black Sea shipping under growing threats as drones hit container ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6115b0f846f2ae1c47db715d78c94532f4882a809012b37633253905e0fd9de0</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:27:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships" /><summary type="html">A Greek container ship has sunk after being struck by three drones, potentially of Russian origin, in the Black Sea off the Bulgarian coast on Wednesday, October 28. This incident highlights growing concerns for commercial shipping as the conflict between Ukraine and Russia persists.</summary></entry><entry><title>'The Phantom of the Opera' haunts French cinemas again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6db412f1112301919e0f8c4b5b2d44fb9f0d883c2bfd768e0a8d6ddd9de41c0f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:24:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261030-the-phantom-of-the-opera-haunts-french-cinemas-again" /><summary type="html">In this edition of arts24, "Le Fantôme de l'Opéra" returns to French cinemas in a contemporary reinterpretation starring Deva Cassel and Romain Duris. We take a closer look.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish transport minister faces calls to quit after deadly train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f665555270bfcd47ae66286451aa11443574f507b20c6a2a84a5b96acda1d240</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:21:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash" /><summary type="html">Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente faced calls to resign but ruled out stepping down on Friday. This follows Wednesday’s train crash in Toledo province, which killed 69 people. It is the country’s second high-speed rail disaster this year. FRANCE 24 correspondent Sarah Morris reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Third weekend of protests looms as tensions persist across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4baac0632cd60f13d71208c7e37900e067272fa41ca27aa46855288297399d06</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:10:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france" /><summary type="html">For the third Saturday in a row, people across France are set to take to the streets to protest against the high cost of living and demand better funding for education. Police are preparing for all eventualities ahead of another weekend of protests, following earlier demonstrations that ended in rioting and looting in city centres.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Kevin T., the main suspect behind the racist Trappes attack?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8433f4e1ce6fbc557ad87b0c52bf60591b3cae9b4b48dfa87869e11cdf46bbe</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack" /><summary type="html">France's anti-terrorism prosecutor on Thursday released details of the main suspect in the racist attack in Trappes and La Verriere, on the outskirts of Paris, on October 23.The 39-year-old opened fire with a submachine gun, killing 26-year-old Pengo Bossio Wangi and injuring five others.</summary></entry><entry><title>How will the women's vote shape the US midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dabb93cf8f953f7437903f5ea6a1858ba3306340ae348c5b3fa9cf6b93981ab</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms approaching, we examine the power of the women's vote in an election that will shape the balance of power in Washington during Donald Trump’s final two years in office. Annette Young talks to Annie Karni, congressional correspondent for The New York Times and Kelly Dittmar, Director of Research at the Centre for American Women and Politics.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>How the record-breaking $6.3 billion heist in crypto history unfolded</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7c5583836ca2b15fcce8c7963de42cfd58cf0554a6e9cdbb78baba6d4bb19d2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261030-how-the-record-breaking-6-3-billion-heist-in-crypto-history-unfolded" /><summary type="html">Hackers stole $6.3 billion in cryptocurrency from Binance in a record-breaking heist, prompting issuers to freeze roughly half of the stolen assets. The breach, which US analysts suspect was done by North Korean hackers, has shaken confidence in the crypto market.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia's European dream left in limbo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b2f892d745eda51cbace27a0419f12b9776c340abad51dc1d6329f49a32ea06</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo" /><summary type="html">Two years ago in Georgia, tens of thousands of pro-European protesters rallied against the disputed results of the October 2024 parliamentary election, which was officially won by the ruling Georgian Dream party. A few weeks later, the authorities announced the suspension of the country's European Union accession process. Despite an ongoing crackdown, smaller-scale protests continue every day in the capital Tbilisi.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Texas Republicans accused of changing electoral rules ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:924db4be13ca137ea3a869a2033022c354c9c28a30f920488c3322f1c1d2127e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:07:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections approaching, Republicans in Texas are being accused of changing electoral rules in their favour. In Tarrant County, near Dallas, they've cut the number of election-day polling places by nearly 30 percent. The decision is being challenged in court and adds to last year's state-wide redistricting, a move designed to benefit Republicans. But the measures could also help galvanise the Democratic opposition. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent reports, with Wassim Cornet.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Ukraine war live: Russian strikes leave 200,000 without power in Ukraine's Dnipropetrovsk region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dfd54147346cc8235eecf5146ab7e2529aad10822e331f130cf0635c9878a21</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:59:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine" /></entry><entry><title>‘Scared of crossing the border’: The Arizona farmers who rely on Mexican workers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:046955afdeef6e6b416ce751e9a0ed7d377aa911fe9aa598faebda1bd88205da</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:28:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers" /><summary type="html">The vast produce farms of Yuma County, Arizona, rely heavily on foreign workers who cross the border every day from Mexico. John Boelts, a farmer and staunch supporter of US President Donald Trump, praises the administration’s strict border controls – though he says that competing Republican factions have complicated efforts to hire foreign labourers.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:791c6dfb6d60d2ea625257eef3d0da20506e925a6bf13c0dbb1d2ac50282174c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers" /><summary type="html">While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Foiled Hindu temple plot exposes rising anti-Indian sentiment in the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ac67ac20cb7ee5ccc632eaa4b8f0eb63c10bcca6cccefe916c1195b798e256e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:02:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261030-foiled-hindu-temple-plot-exposes-rising-anti-indian-sentiment-in-the-us" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Access Asia, we explore why anti-Indian sentiment is rising in the United States in the wake of the foiled plot targeting a Hindu temple in Illinois. We ask the executive director of the Center for the Study of Organized Hate what's behind the trend, and whether the rhetoric coming from the Trump White House is to blame.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>At least 60 Christians killed in Ethiopia amid rising religious violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a39422e830bf3f060a8f356a1d2bf95b17dc62a900fe4698f2678505b3787beb</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence" /><summary type="html">At least 60 Christians have been killed in Ethiopia in what the Orthodox Church has declared as religious violence. It is still unclear who was behind the attack, with rebels and local government blaming each other. Around 20 houses have been burned down, as FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal gears up for historic 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Dakar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb6df477c1241ea915a5cc8e56d4ddb2d2f91ff75d14122f6d2afb439dd72725</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee is upbeat just 24 hours before competition gets under way at the 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Senegal. Venues are ready to host the first-ever Olympic event on the African continent. FRANCE 24's correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tanzania: 2025 election violence still traumatises, one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f81be675cc78c28188886f1195dea292dcaa38896dce54322b6fb526bec624ce</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:55:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">Tanzania is marking the first anniversary of a bloody election that left many traumatised. The October 29, 2025 election, in which President Samia Suluhu Hassan won with 98 percent of the vote after most of the opposition was excluded, triggered days of protests that security forces brutally suppressed. Many government critics say they still fear abduction, arbitrary arrest and politically motivated prosecutions.</summary></entry><entry><title>TotalEnergies posts record profits as it keeps a lid on fuel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b4fac4a052c4705727401a4af4940f7f0ce80af0ef9c240c00af556fa96020c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:40:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-totalenergies-posts-record-profits-as-it-keeps-a-lid-on-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">As hundreds of thousands across France are expected to take to the street again this weekend to protest the high cost of living, oil and gas giant TotalEnergies has posted record profits for the quarter to September. The company has kept fuel prices lower than rivals at its pumps, but motorists are wondering whether it could bring them lower still.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tennis: Alexander Zverev guaranteed to become world No. 1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0861bafe78d04e448fd281548860a472ae3ef9365c562ae9612ca4b892b73052</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:34:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261030-tennis-alexander-zverev-guaranteed-to-become-world-no-1" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev secured his place as the next world No. 1 by beating Tallon Griekspoor (6-4, 7-5) at the ATP 500 tournament in Vienna. The 29-year-old German will top the ATP rankings on Monday, November 2, replacing Jannik Sinner. He will become the first German world No. 1 since Boris Becker in 1991, and the 30th player in history to reach the top spot.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Israel elections: Netanyahu attacks Arab parties as they emerge as potential kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:646d3e1360fc3b7593d9bb424ceb87cafb91b6fec9002ff471267fe903a4e26a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:10:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-elections-netanyahu-attacks-arab-parties-as-they-emerge-as-potential-kingmakers" /><summary type="html">Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud party alleged on Thursday, without ​providing evidence, that Arab parties' record gains in an election this week were driven in part by voter fraud. These accusations represent an escalation of anti-Arab rhetoric by Netanyahu and his far-right partners after Arab-led parties made a historic showing in the election – giving them a potential kingmaker role in the next government</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel elections: Difficult negotiations lie ahead after Netanyahu's bloc lost majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a17ea1b3b26d9356a440df3cd064dbe8f9d4564472bef576a8c7c7adb03b8670</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-elections-difficult-negotiations-lie-ahead-after-netanyahu-s-bloc-lost-majority" /><summary type="html">Israel's final election results confirmed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s bloc lost its majority of parliamentary seats and that weeks of difficult negotiations among very different parties, from ultra-Orthodox Jewish to secular to Arab-led, lie ahead. The results released early Friday showed Netanyahu’s bloc won 53 seats in Tuesday's elections. The main opposition bloc won 48. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain demands answers as train disaster toll rises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a3d2eb3de1e11c32a2271f3dd6ea32c686273357dd0296bab448b12edbdb588</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:05:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spain-demands-answers-as-train-disaster-toll-rises" /><summary type="html">Spain began demanding answers on Thursday after the toll from the country's second high-speed train collision this year rose to 69 people, with scores injured and distraught relatives desperately seeking news about their loved ones. One of Europe's deadliest rail disasters this century struck south of Madrid on Wednesday morning when a service by state operator Renfe ploughed into the back of a stationary train belonging to private Spanish company Iryo. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: With deep-red states now in play, could blue wave redraw America's political landscape?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f87ad978639671ea3f6914ca03a66b2a6e27f1e9478d1af24295f15d02385a1a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T09:30:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape" /><summary type="html">With the US approaching a potentially consequential midterm election, the political landscape appears to be shifting. Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Dr Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics &amp; Policy at Queen Mary University of London, who examines the prospect of a sweeping Democratic victory. He argues that the party could achieve gains of a magnitude not seen since Barack Obama's historic presidential election in 2008. Johnson sees a combination of Democratic enthusiasm, and growing support among independents, white college-educated voters and Latinos, and signs of defections from Donald Trump's fiercely loyal electoral coalition.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's bastion of free press Novaya Gazeta shuts down under Kremlin pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48e7269cb9e201b7840b232957acde9aad7f78f807d8d73b5e6bdecf538f5b5a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:42:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-russia-s-bastion-of-free-press-novaya-gazeta-shuts-down-after-years-of-kremlin-pressure" /><summary type="html">Newspaper Novaya Gazeta, one of the last vestiges of independent journalism in Russia, announced Friday that it was closing down, citing pressure from authorities who recently searched the home of its senior editor and earlier this year detained one of its journalists.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
